Projects/UOContent/Engines/Craft/DefInscription.cs

Adds DefInscription.Knows, a static hook a caller may set to let a mobile write a spell it does not hold in a book.
Null — as the engine leaves it — keeps the rule that the spell must be in the scribe's own book. The circle's skill
gate (minimum Inscribe of -25, -10.8, 3.5, 17.8, 32.1, 46.4, 60.7 and 75 for the eight circles, no chance at the bottom
of each band) is asked either way. Without this patch BotAIv2 does not compile.

WHY. Patrick's order of 25.09.2026: "make a gradation of writing scrolls — the higher the Inscribe, the stronger the
scrolls they can write". Above the third circle no shop sells a scroll, and the engine refuses to write one whose spell
is not in the scribe's book, so a fourth-circle spell reached the population only off a corpse: 358 wants for Lightning
in two days, one of them filled, the rest holding the mages' money down for an hour each. BotAIv2 sets the hook to
"any bot" (BotSpellsModule.Start) and clears it on a reload; players are untouched.

